 'kana-sisters':{type:'branches',titleAr:'عَمَلُ كَانَ وَأَخَوَاتِهَا',titleEn:'How kāna and its sisters work',branches:[
  {id:'kana-ordinary',labelAr:'الْعَمَلُ الْأَصْلِيُّ',labelEn:'Core operation',descAr:'تَرْفَعُ الِاسْمَ وَتَنْصِبُ الْخَبَرَ: «وَكَانَ اللَّهُ غَفُورًا رَحِيمًا».',descEn:'They raise the ism and make the khabar accusative, as in wa-kāna Allāhu ghafūran raḥīman.',exerciseId:'kana-01'},
  {id:'kana-conditional-sisters',labelAr:'بَعْدَ نَفْيٍ أَوْ نَهْيٍ أَوْ دُعَاءٍ',labelEn:'After negation, prohibition, or supplication',descAr:'يَعْمَلُ «زَالَ» وَ«فَتِئَ» وَ«بَرِحَ» وَ«انْفَكَّ» بِهَذَا الشَّرْطِ: «وَلَا يَزَالُونَ مُخْتَلِفِينَ».',descEn:'Zāla, fatiʾa, bariḥa, and infakka operate under this condition, as in wa-lā yazālūna mukhtalifīna.',exerciseId:'kana-05'},
  {id:'kana-dama',labelAr:'«دَامَ» بَعْدَ «مَا»',labelEn:'Dāma after mā',descAr:'تَعْمَلُ «دَامَ» بَعْدَ «مَا» الْمَصْدَرِيَّةِ الظَّرْفِيَّةِ: «مَا دُمْتُ حَيًّا».',descEn:'Dāma operates after temporal source-forming mā, as in mā dumtu ḥayyan.',exerciseId:'kana-09'},
  {id:'kana-order',labelAr:'تَقْدِيمُ الْخَبَرِ وَتَوَسُّطُهُ',labelEn:'Fronting and intervening khabar',descAr:'يَتَوَسَّطُ الْخَبَرُ بَيْنَ الْفِعْلِ وَاسْمِهِ: «وَكَانَ حَقًّا عَلَيْنَا نَصْرُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ».',descEn:'The khabar may stand between the verb and its ism.',exerciseId:'kana-10'},
  {id:'kana-complete',labelAr:'كَانَ التَّامَّةُ',labelEn:'Complete kāna',descAr:'تَكْتَفِي بِفَاعِلٍ وَلَا تَحْتَاجُ إِلَى خَبَرٍ: «وَإِنْ كَانَ ذُو عُسْرَةٍ».',descEn:'Complete kāna takes a subject and needs no khabar.',exerciseId:'kana-15'},
  {id:'kana-special',labelAr:'خَصَائِصُ كَانَ',labelEn:'Special properties of kāna',descAr:'تَزِيدُ «كَانَ» أَوْ تُحْذَفُ هِيَ وَاسْمُهَا فِي الْمَوَاضِعِ الَّتِي ذَكَرَهَا الْمُؤَلِّفُ، وَقَدْ تُحْذَفُ نُونُ مُضَارِعِهَا الْمَجْزُومِ.',descEn:'Kāna may be extra, or it and its ism may be omitted in the stated environments; the nūn of its jussive present may also be deleted.',children:[
   {id:'kana-extra',labelAr:'كَانَ الزَّائِدَةُ',labelEn:'Extra kāna',descAr:'«مَا كَانَ أَحْسَنَ زَيْدًا»: «كَانَ» زَائِدَةٌ بَيْنَ مُتَلَازِمَيْنِ.',descEn:'In mā kāna aḥsana Zaydan, kāna is extra between two closely connected elements.',exerciseId:'kana-17'},
   {id:'kana-omitted',labelAr:'حَذْفُ كَانَ وَاسْمِهَا',labelEn:'Omitting kāna and its ism',descAr:'«الْتَمِسْ وَلَوْ خَاتَمًا»: حُذِفَتْ «كَانَ» وَاسْمُهَا وَبَقِيَ خَبَرُهَا.',descEn:'In iltamis wa-law khātaman, kāna and its ism are omitted while its khabar remains.',exerciseId:'kana-18'},
   {id:'kana-nun-deletion',labelAr:'حَذْفُ النُّونِ',labelEn:'Deleting nūn',descAr:'تُحْذَفُ نُونُ مُضَارِعِ «كَانَ» الْمَجْزُومِ تَخْفِيفًا بِالشُّرُوطِ الْمَذْكُورَةِ، وَتَبْقَى عَلَامَةُ الْجَزْمِ السُّكُونَ عَلَى النُّونِ الْمَحْذُوفَةِ.',descEn:'The nūn of jussive yakun may be deleted for lightness under the stated conditions; the sign remains sukūn on the deleted nūn.',children:[
    {id:'kana-nun-lam',labelAr:'«وَلَمْ أَكُ بَغِيًّا»',labelEn:'After jussive lam',descAr:'أَصْلُ «أَكُ»: «أَكُونُ»، فَحُذِفَتِ الْوَاوُ لِلْجَزْمِ، ثُمَّ حُذِفَتِ النُّونُ تَخْفِيفًا.',descEn:'Aku comes from akūnu: the weak letter is deleted for jazm, then nūn is deleted for lightness.',exerciseId:'kana-20'},
    {id:'kana-nun-prohibition',labelAr:'«وَلَا تَكُ فِي ضَيْقٍ»',labelEn:'After prohibitive lā',descAr:'«تَكُ» مَجْزُومٌ بِـ«لَا» النَّاهِيَةِ، وَنُونُهُ مَحْذُوفَةٌ تَخْفِيفًا.',descEn:'Taku is jussive after prohibitive lā, with its nūn deleted for lightness.',exerciseId:'kana-21'},
    {id:'kana-nun-condition',labelAr:'«وَإِنْ تَكُ حَسَنَةً»',labelEn:'After conditional in',descAr:'«تَكُ» فِعْلُ الشَّرْطِ مَجْزُومٌ، وَنُونُهُ مَحْذُوفَةٌ تَخْفِيفًا.',descEn:'Taku is the jussive condition verb, with its nūn deleted for lightness.',exerciseId:'kana-22'}
   ]}
  ]}
 ]}
